**NIX BUNDLE APP WITH RESOURCE FILES**  
A NIX bundle is a way to package and distribute applications and their resources in a self-contained format. When you create a NIX bundle, you include all the necessary files, such as code, configuration, and resources, in a single file. This makes it easy to distribute and run the app on any system that has NIX installed.

**EXAMPLE**  
Suppose you have an app called "GOLF" that needs to access a configuration file called "config.nix". You would create a NIX bundle that includes both the app code and the configuration file. The bundle would look something like this:

```nix
{
  name = "golf-app";
  version = "1.0.0";
  inputs = {
    config = {
      url = "https://example.com/config.nix";
      sha256 = "sha256-abc123";
    };
  };
}
```

In this example, the "GOLF" app is bundled with its configuration file, which is stored at "https://example.com/config.nix". The bundle includes all the necessary files to run the app, including the configuration.

